    "funFacts": [
     "هٰؤُلَاءِ and أُولٰئِكَ share أُولَاءِ: هَا- in front makes it near (“these”), -كَ behind makes it far (“those”)."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "Only for people: “these books” is هٰذِهِ الْكُتُبُ, not *هٰؤُلَاءِ الْكُتُبُ.",
     "Written with a dagger alif and a hamza on wāw; the final -i never changes: هٰؤُلَاءِ (hāʾulāʾi)."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "The same word serves men and women: هٰؤُلَاءِ الطَّالِبَاتُ (these female students)."
